{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSVuYX1DfJPbeB4MHVV8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have a complete understanding of the codebase. Let me move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add a new endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Takes the shipmentId as a path variable\n   - Finds the shipment in the repository\n   - Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the shipment doesn't exist (404)\n   - Throws `ConflictException` if the shipment status is CANCELLED (409)\n   - Updates the status to CONFIRMED if it's CREATED (or leaves it unchanged if already CONFIRMED for idempotency)\n   - Saves the shipment and returns it with 200 OK status\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** - Add a new error code `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` for the case when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add 5 new test cases covering:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment transitions it to CONFIRMED\n   - Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and changes nothing (idempotency)\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with the error code\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n   - The response body contains the correct shipment status after confirmation\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED):**\n  - POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm\n  - Repository.findById(shipmentId) → Shipment with status=CREATED\n  - Create new Shipment with status=CONFIRMED\n  - Repository.save(updated shipment)\n  - Return 200 OK with updated Shipment\n\n- **Idempotent path (already CONFIRMED):**\n  - POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm\n  - Repository.findById(shipmentId) → Shipment with status=CONFIRMED\n  - Check if status is CANCELLED (it's not)\n  - Return the shipment unchanged with 200 OK\n\n- **Conflict path (CANCELLED):**\n  - POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm\n  - Repository.findById(shipmentId) → Shipment with status=CANCELLED\n  - Throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED, message)\n  - GlobalExceptionHandler catches it\n  - Return 409 with ApiError envelope\n\n- **Not found path:**\n  - POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm\n  - Repository.findById(shipmentId) → null\n  - Throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message)\n  - GlobalExceptionHandler catches it\n  - Return 404 with ApiError envelope\n\n**Alternatives considered and rejected:**\n\n1. **Alternative: Adding a service layer** - The existing code doesn't have a service layer between controller and repository; all logic is in the controller. Following the existing pattern, the logic should stay in the controller.\n\n2. **Alternative: Using PUT instead of POST** - The ticket specifically asks for POST. POST is appropriate here because it's an action endpoint (confirm) rather than a full resource replacement, which would use PUT.\n\n3. **Alternative: Not distinguishing between not found and cancelled** - The ticket requires returning 409 for cancelled, making it essential to differentiate. Returning 404 would make it indistinguishable from a non-existent shipment, which is poor API design.\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Confirm CREATED shipment - verifies transition happens\n- Test 2: Confirm already CONFIRMED shipment - verifies idempotency\n- Test 3: Confirm CANCELLED shipment - verifies 409 response with correct error code\n- Test 4: Confirm non-existent shipment - verifies 404 response with correct error code\n- Test 5: Response body check - verifies the returned shipment has the correct status\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. First, let me add the new error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":868,"cache_read_input_tokens":21756,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":868},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"975b2ba5-7be5-4669-ab27-368ff0ffecba","uuid":"71b41428-a962-4e1d-bafd-ae8755af3d96","timestamp":"2026-09-26T18:09:31.368Z","request_id":"req_011CfSVuY3y1HfF6nHmgcMaW"}
