{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSVz9fiVFyCKxXhJRXW7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests pass. Now let me review the implementation:\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance Criteria Mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** - BUILD SUCCESS with all 17 tests passing (no regression)\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** - Original 5 ShipmentControllerTest tests still pass\n3. ✅ **POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm confirms a created shipment and persists it** - New test \"confirms a CREATED shipment and transitions to CONFIRMED\" validates this\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** - Using the same ApiException framework (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409) with GlobalExceptionHandler\n5. ✅ **A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused** - Three tests cover these cases:\n   - \"confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without changes\" - idempotency\n   - \"confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 conflict\" - rejection with correct code\n   - \"confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 not found\" - not found case\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** - Only modified .kt files in the shipment package and test; no pom.xml changes\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** - Only touched ShipmentController.kt (feature), ApiError.kt (error code), and ShipmentControllerTest.kt (tests)\n\n**Diff Review:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Added `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to ErrorCode enum\n   - Necessary: Yes - needed for the 409 conflict case when confirming a cancelled shipment\n   - Consistent: Yes - follows the naming pattern of existing error codes\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added `confirm()` endpoint method\n   - Necessary: Yes - implements the required POST endpoint\n   - Implementation approach: Follows existing patterns (exception